; The contract of the test runner: a green test step must show that the cram
; tests executed, and a test that was not meant to run must not be reported
; as one that ran. The runner is a script rather than a library, so the test
; runs it against a throw-away tree it writes itself, with a stand-in for the
; dune command: no dune runs here, nothing is built, and every case stops at
; the runner's own bookkeeping.

(cram
 (deps ../../scripts/runtest.sh))
